{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2568aaa204dd2d1b","type":"group","x":-40,"y":280,"width":1720,"height":980,"label":"01 · ARRIVAL AND TRIAGE — treat immediate danger first"},
		{"id":"b48ab14c941506c9","type":"group","x":-40,"y":1340,"width":1720,"height":1160,"label":"02 · ASSESSMENT — assemble the evidence in parallel"},
		{"id":"4f3b6b822f6a8e87","type":"group","x":-40,"y":2580,"width":1720,"height":1020,"label":"03 · CLASSIFICATION — determine which problem needs care"},
		{"id":"bc4ae8d5e7f6d2e7","type":"group","x":-40,"y":3700,"width":1720,"height":1080,"label":"04 · DISPOSITION — match the next step to the remaining risk"},
		{"id":"aaf2320646108059","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":1640,"height":260,"text":"# SYNCOPE IN THE EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT\n## The EUSEM 2024 pathway — explained\n**Read downwards; follow labelled side branches.** Original educational redraw based on Möckel et al., Figs. 2–3. Blue: assessment · yellow: decision · red: urgent/disease-specific care · green: low-risk destination · purple: explanation.\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained|Open the detailed companion note and references]] · **Integrated Spanish version (ESC, EUSEM, UpToDate, NEJM…):** [[30_Urgencias/Patologia_Aguda/Síncope en Urgencias - Flujograma.canvas|Síncope en Urgencias — Flujograma]]","color":"6"},
		{"id":"2ba137ba3df58ba7","type":"text","x":580,"y":340,"width":480,"height":220,"text":"## 1 · Apparent TLOC / presyncope\nObtain the patient and witness account. Begin triage.\n\n**Do not assume syncope yet.** Persistent altered consciousness needs a broader assessment.\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#1 — Start with the event|Read the explanation →]]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"ad12f62c45fc1344","type":"text","x":580,"y":650,"width":480,"height":200,"text":"## 2a · Trauma caused TLOC?\nEstablish the sequence: primary head injury, or collapse followed by injury?\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#2 — Separate trauma and shock early|Read the explanation →]]","color":"3"},
		{"id":"4fe6edce8f4508d2","type":"text","x":0,"y":650,"width":480,"height":250,"text":"## Traumatic-TLOC pathway\nPrioritise injury assessment and treatment.\n\nIf injury followed a faint, investigate **both the injury and the collapse**. Finding trauma does not explain the preceding event.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"74cac794aefecdbb","type":"text","x":580,"y":960,"width":480,"height":200,"text":"## 2b · Shock / immediate instability?\nRecognise and treat instability immediately. These checks may overlap in real care.\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#2 — Separate trauma and shock early|Read the explanation →]]","color":"3"},
		{"id":"7e073ac88af99a91","type":"text","x":1160,"y":960,"width":480,"height":250,"text":"## Resuscitation / shock pathway\nTreat the immediate physiological threat and its cause.\n\nThe paper highlights sepsis; it does not imply that every case of shock is septic.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"f379ccb92b911644","type":"text","x":580,"y":1400,"width":480,"height":150,"text":"## Nontraumatic TLOC without shock\nThis is a working description, not yet an aetiological diagnosis.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"e6978aa4de206ac1","type":"text","x":0,"y":1660,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 3a · Vital signs\nBP · heart rate · oxygen saturation · respiratory rate · temperature.\n\nReview triage measurements, repeat as needed and document.\n\n**Normal now does not explain earlier.** [1, Table 1]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#3 — Establish the initial clinical picture|Read the explanation →]]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"180e2a602c511ee7","type":"text","x":580,"y":1660,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 3b · 12-lead ECG\nAcquire, interpret and document.\n\n**EUSEM target: qualified interpretation within 10 minutes of registration.**\n\nLook for dangerous rhythm, conduction or ischaemic findings. [1, Table 3]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#3 — Establish the initial clinical picture|Read the explanation →]]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"26cb941323ef3be9","type":"text","x":1160,"y":1660,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 3c · Directed blood tests\nGlucose + haemoglobin are the paper’s minimum **where indicated by the setting**.\n\nAdditional tests follow clinical suspicion. The table is not a universal panel. [1, Table 2]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#3 — Establish the initial clinical picture|Read the explanation →]]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"259aa8ef98a8b91d","type":"text","x":580,"y":2100,"width":480,"height":330,"text":"## 4 · Complete the clinical assessment\n**Before:** posture, activity, triggers, prodrome.\n**During:** witness account and injury.\n**After:** recovery and persistent symptoms.\n\nReview history, medications and examination. Consider active standing when suitable. [1, part 2]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#4 — Reconstruct the episode and consider orthostasis|Read the explanation →]]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"600c5f8e57a0549a","type":"text","x":0,"y":2100,"width":480,"height":330,"text":"## Read the findings together\nA normal ECG cannot exclude an intermittent arrhythmia.\n\nAn abnormal result does not necessarily establish causation.\n\nA postural BP fall must fit the event.\n\n**Interpretation:** each test answers one question, not the whole presentation.","color":"6"},
		{"id":"336074805fc85398","type":"text","x":1160,"y":2100,"width":480,"height":330,"text":"## Sequence is flexible; priorities are not\nHistory, examination and stabilisation begin as needed — do not wait for blood results.\n\nIf new instability or a serious diagnosis emerges, leave the generic pathway and act on it.\n\n**Teaching note:** the diagram organises care; it does not delay it.","color":"6"},
		{"id":"fc1f263d32b8ed4a","type":"text","x":580,"y":2640,"width":480,"height":200,"text":"## 5 · What explains the event?\nIntegrate the initial assessment.\nKeep the diagnosis open to revision.\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#5 — Decide which problem you are treating|Read the explanation →]]","color":"3"},
		{"id":"692e51978c0e4aa1","type":"text","x":0,"y":2640,"width":480,"height":240,"text":"## Not syncope / still unclear?\nReassess for seizures, psychogenic TLOC, trauma or another disorder of consciousness.\n\n**Do not force an uncertain event into a syncope risk category.** [1, part 3]","color":"6"},
		{"id":"6f4f1b1c9d25ee4a","type":"text","x":0,"y":2960,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## A · Another illness dominates\nExamples in the paper: pulmonary embolism, aortic dissection, sepsis without shock.\n\n**Enter the disease-specific pathway.** Treat the underlying illness.\n\n[1, part 2]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#5 — Decide which problem you are treating|Read the explanation →]]","color":"1"},
		{"id":"96642b36a83c4c78","type":"text","x":580,"y":2960,"width":480,"height":230,"text":"## C · Likely syncope, uncertain cause\nA working diagnosis of syncope is plausible; the precise mechanism remains unresolved.\n\n**Proceed to risk assessment.**","color":"3"},
		{"id":"7117fff2d0fd2944","type":"text","x":1160,"y":2960,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## B · Cause certain / highly likely\nPaper examples: aortic stenosis or complete heart block.\n\n**Enter the cause-specific pathway.**\nA known cause can be dangerous; certainty does not imply safe discharge. [1, part 2]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#5 — Decide which problem you are treating|Read the explanation →]]","color":"1"},
		{"id":"2c6ef0f0d0e4cc6e","type":"text","x":580,"y":3330,"width":480,"height":220,"text":"## 6 · What risk remains?\nAssess the **event + medical history + examination + ECG** using ESC categories.\n\nUnexplained does not mean low risk. [1, part 3]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#6 — Stratify risk without confusing it with certainty|Read the explanation →]]","color":"3"},
		{"id":"6c1ff09db3a73dc4","type":"text","x":0,"y":3780,"width":480,"height":230,"text":"## LOW RISK\nThe overall assessment supports a low-risk presentation.\n\nNo diagnosis or single test grants this label automatically.\n\n[1, part 3]","color":"4"},
		{"id":"94e6f02a5aca51e4","type":"text","x":580,"y":3780,"width":480,"height":230,"text":"## INTERMEDIATE RISK\nNeither clearly low nor high risk.\n\n**The EUSEM paper calls for further evaluation and monitoring, not direct discharge at this point.** [1, part 3]","color":"2"},
		{"id":"6ef7c9b15ecdd690","type":"text","x":1160,"y":3780,"width":480,"height":230,"text":"## HIGH RISK\nFeatures suggest a potentially serious underlying condition.\n\n**Urgent monitored evaluation** and treatment as indicated. [1, part 3]","color":"1"},
		{"id":"a4ac536145d6649d","type":"text","x":0,"y":4140,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 7a · Discharge pathway\nDischarge according to local practice with appropriate outpatient follow-up. [1]\n\n**Practical application:** document the assessment, explain the likely cause or uncertainty, and give advice, safety-netting and follow-up.\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#7 — Make the disposition understandable|Read the explanation →]]","color":"4"},
		{"id":"74e892c91130daa5","type":"text","x":580,"y":4140,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 7b · Observation / further work-up\nContinue assessment and monitoring in an appropriate ED or hospital-based setting. [1]\n\nReassess before deciding on discharge or further care.\n\n**No fixed monitoring duration is established by this paper.**\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#7 — Make the disposition understandable|Read the explanation →]]","color":"2"},
		{"id":"f9d37c23fcc0f03c","type":"text","x":1160,"y":4140,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"## 7c · Urgent monitored care\nHospital-based evaluation and treatment according to the concern. [1]\n\n**ESC context:** suitable observation or specialist pathways may replace an inpatient bed in selected cases; admit when required care cannot safely be delivered there. [2]\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#6 — Stratify risk without confusing it with certainty|Read the explanation →]]","color":"1"},
		{"id":"df09e9cc59fb4d30","type":"text","x":0,"y":4540,"width":1640,"height":180,"text":"## Reassess throughout — this is a consensus pathway, not an outcome trial\nA new finding can change both the diagnosis and the destination. The original process is intended for local adaptation; no universal observation time or exhaustive treatment protocol is provided. **Every exit means continuation of appropriate care.**\n\n[[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#9 — What the paper establishes, and what it does not|Study methods and limitations]] · [[30_Urgencias/Syncope-EUSEM-2024/Syncope-EUSEM-2024-explained#References and source map|Sources and page-level references]]","color":"6"},
		{"id":"e812cd2db8f94909","type":"text","x":0,"y":4880,"width":1640,"height":210,"text":"## Sources\n**[1] Möckel et al., EUSEM 2024.** *The syncope core management process in the emergency department.* Figs. 2–3; Tables 1–3; pp. 253–258. DOI: [10.1097/MEJ.0000000000001146](https://doi.org/10.1097/MEJ.0000000000001146).\n\n**[2] Brignole et al., ESC 2018.** §4.1.2, Fig. 6 and Table 7. DOI: [10.1093/eurheartj/ehy037](https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehy037). Added disposition context is explicitly labelled.\n\nPrepared 27 October 2026 · English learning companion · Not a locally approved protocol.","color":"6"}
	],
